\v 1 A cross reference\x + \xo 4.1: \xt 1 Sam 31.4; 2 Sam 1.1\x* sits mid-verse. This verse ends with a footnote butted against the next verse marker with no space between them.\f + \fr 4.1 \ft A footnote that ends right before the next verse marker.\f*
\v 2-3 \vp 2-3a\vp* Verse bridge 2-3 carrying a published verse number (vp).
\v 4a Verse segment 4a.
\v 4b Verse segment 4b.
\v 5 An endnote\fe + \fr 4.5 \ft Endnote text.\fe* then a footnote with no caller\f - \fr 4.5 \ft The minus caller means no caller is shown.\f* then one with a custom caller\f a \fr 4.5 \ft Custom caller a.\f* end.
\v 6 Non-breaking spaces: a character span whose whole content is a NBSP \nd ~\nd*, one with a leading NBSP \nd ~lead\nd*, one with a trailing NBSP \nd trail~\nd*, a NBSP before punctuation mot~: and one inside a number 1~000.
\p ~
\p The paragraph above has a lone NBSP as its only content. This paragraph ends with a space before an unknown marker \zunk Unknown marker content.
